---
const en = Astro.props.lang === "en";
const t=(a:string,b:string)=>en?a:b;
---
<h2>{t("How many dances fit one sentence?", "一句话可以跳出多少支舞？")}</h2>
<p>{t("Ask two dancers to step sideways and turn with their arms out. Both can follow the instruction while planting different feet, opening their arms at different times and finishing at different angles. A recording settles every one of those choices. The sentence settles only a few. That gap matters when we turn motion into tokens: the decoder sees a particular performance, while a text-conditioned generator has to learn the space of possible performances.", "请两个人各跳一遍“侧步，张开双臂转身”。一个人可能先迈右脚，借着摆臂转过去；另一个人会先把重心压低，脚跟转开后才舒展肩膀。两个人都读懂了这句话。动捕记下的是其中一次表演，每一帧都有确定的答案。文字给出的答案却有很多种。把动作压成离散 token 时，哪些选择值得留给生成器？")}</p>
<h2>{t("One packet carries intent and detail", "同一个动作包里装什么？")}</h2>
<p>{t("In the published SeMoCo architecture a short interval of motion becomes one packet. Its first discrete code is trained to agree with a semantic teacher. The remaining codes describe kinematic detail. A decoder uses both to recover the motion. The teacher supplies a learning signal during training. Individual code IDs have no assigned human-readable label.", "公开论文中的 SeMoCo 把一小段时间内的身体运动压成一个包。包头是一个离散的语义码，训练时用教师模型的表示来约束它；后面的运动学码逐级补充细节，解码器再从两部分恢复动作。这里的“语义”指训练信号。研究者并没有给某个编号起名叫“转身”，也不能看一眼编号就读出舞步。")}</p>
<p>{t("For the dance, the distinction is easy to feel: the turn can still read as a turn when the dancer opens an elbow a moment later. The encoder has to preserve enough geometry to recover that elbow path while organizing packets so a generator can learn which movements plausibly follow a side step.", "可以用手肘来理解这个取舍。舞者晚半拍打开手肘，我们大多仍能认出转身；可要还原这一次表演，晚半拍就很重要。一个好的动作包既要给解码器留下这条手肘轨迹，也要让生成器有机会学到侧步之后哪些动作接得上。")}</p>
<h2>{t("Two predictions at different scales", "接下来跳什么，这一拍怎么跳？")}</h2>
<p>{t("The temporal Transformer reads earlier packets and predicts the next semantic code. A smaller depth decoder takes that temporal state and code, then predicts the kinematic codes in order within the packet. Sampling advances one packet and repeats. In the paper’s 50 Hz configuration one packet covers four frames, so the temporal model advances 12.5 times a second. The depth decoder can resolve detail within each interval without adding more steps to the temporal sequence.", "时间轴上的 Transformer 读取此前的动作包，预测下一包的语义码。较小的深度解码器拿到这一刻的上下文和语义码，依次生成包内的运动学码，然后模型再向前走一包。论文中的 50 Hz 配置每四帧打一个包，时间模型每秒推进 12.5 次。细节可以在同一个时间位置逐层补上，不必把每一个码都当成新的一拍。")}</p>
<h2>{t("What changes when language shapes the representation?","引入语言监督后，哪些指标发生了变化？")}</h2>
<p>{t("Table 5 of the public SeMoCo paper compares two split-branch tokenizers paired with the same 150M Flan-T5 generator. Enabling semantic supervision changes how well generated motions match the text, as well as how closely a reconstructed skeleton follows the recording.","SeMoCo 公开论文的表 5 中，有两组配置都使用分支式 tokenizer，配合同样的 150M Flan-T5 生成器。加入语义监督后，生成动作和文本的匹配度发生变化，重建骨架与原始记录的距离也随之改变。")}</p>
<p>{t("Read the three columns as different questions. FID measures the distance between generated and recorded motion distributions in the evaluator’s embedding space. R@1 asks how often a caption retrieves its paired motion first among the candidates. MPJPE compares corresponding joints after encoding and decoding an actual recording. Only the last measure asks for exactly the same performance back.", "表里的三个数各有一个观察对象。FID 比较生成动作与真实动作在评估器特征空间中的分布；R@1 看一条文字能否从候选动作中把配对的那一条排在首位；MPJPE 则把同一段动捕送去编码、解码，再逐关节测量与原始姿态相差多少毫米。只有最后一项要求找回同一次表演。")}</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>{t("Semantic supervision","语义监督")}</th><th>FID ↓</th><th>R@1 ↑</th><th>MPJPE-77 ↓</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>{t("Off","关闭")}</th><td>0.226</td><td>0.319</td><td>13.70 mm</td></tr><tr><th>{t("On","开启")}</th><td>0.186</td><td>0.484</td><td>15.93 mm</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>{t("For these two configurations the additional 2.23 mm of average joint error accompanies better generation FID and higher top-one text retrieval. Selecting solely by reconstruction would pick the other model. For a text-driven application, evaluate the representation with its generator attached; for motion archival, measure what survives decoding.","在这两组配置中，平均关节误差增加了 2.23 毫米，同时生成 FID 降低，文本检索首位命中率上升。如果只按重建误差选模型，选择会恰好相反。给文字生成动作时，应把表示和下游生成器一起评估；要存档某位表演者的动作，则应检查解码后保住了哪些细节。")}</p>
<h2>{t("Would the same supervision help any tokenizer?", "语义监督放在哪里都有效吗？")}</h2>
<p>{t("Table 5 includes a useful counterexample. With a single residual chain, adding semantic supervision moved FID from 0.202 to 0.211 and top-one retrieval from 0.483 to 0.451. Both means moved in the opposite direction from the split-branch experiment. The plain chain also retained the best top-two through top-five retrieval. The arrangement of the codes matters when interpreting what the teacher contributed.", "表 5 还做了一个容易忽略的对照。把码排成单条残差链时，同样打开语义监督，FID 从 0.202 变为 0.211，首位检索命中率从 0.483 变为 0.451。两个均值的变化方向都与分支配置相反。朴素的单链甚至保留了最好的前二至前五命中率。只说“加入语义就更好”，会漏掉这个实验最值得保留的条件：教师信号加在怎样的表示结构上？")}</p>
<p>{t("The table averages 30 repeats, with separate generation pools rather than matched performances. It can tell us how configurations behaved across a collection. It cannot tell us which model placed a particular dancer’s foot more convincingly. For that question, keep the caption and viewing conditions fixed, sample several takes and inspect the timing and contact of the feet alongside the retrieval and reconstruction scores.", "表里的生成指标取三十次重复的均值，各配置采样出的舞者和舞步并非逐条配对。因此，这组结果适合回答哪种表示更适合一批文本生成任务。若关心具体一段舞有没有踩实地面，可以固定提示词和机位，多生成几次，回看落脚时刻，再结合检索和重建指标判断。项目页的舞蹈回放就保留了同一份人体动作，切换机器人时可以停在同一拍观察。")}</p>
<p><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.24334">{t("SeMoCo paper · Table 5","SeMoCo 公开论文 · 表 5")} ↗</a></p>
<style>table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:clamp(.78rem,2vw,1rem)}th,td{text-align:left;padding:.7em .35em;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}</style>
